# M1 platform benchmarker and CI

Complete the M1 platform benchmark runner and test runner against the working code, reusing existing implementation. Follow your current M1 design-package: `benchmark-runner.md`, `automation.md`, and the `README.md` files titled **AI4Research sidecar container** and **Test runner (client validation in the sidecar container)**. These documents own the detailed contracts. The explicitly requested OpenJiuwen baseline adapter below is additional delivery scope; it does not redefine the core M1 acceptance gate.

The platform benchmarker submits frozen, versioned cases, observes runs and retrieves permitted exports to establish a comparable M1 system baseline. It is distinct from the Research Benchmark CC inside a research run. Separate processes perform referee scoring against protected labels and report generation; the benchmark runner never scores or treats product-verifier verdicts as ground truth.

Run both client roles as finite sidecar jobs, with separate scoped tokens. Connect through Compose service DNS and container port `app:5173` by default, never the sidecar's localhost. Verify readiness, target/build identity, client-contract compatibility and prerequisites before submission. Use supported control API/export operations; reconcile uncertain submissions without blind resubmission. No app-volume access, Docker socket, hidden labels or privileged product-state writes. Optional bounded host operations remain with the host launcher. Product startup/research runs remain independent of the sidecar, and the benchmark pilot does not gate core M1 acceptance.

Implement the design's `test-runner` commands via `docker compose run --rm sidecar test-runner <command>`. Run the complete sequential `matrix` before merge; only exit 0 permits merge, with no skipped cases. Preserve the specified exits: 0 met, 1 mismatch, 2 blocked, 3 inconclusive; matrix returns the highest case code. This client has no evaluation-profile entry-point authority. Keep mock and model-backed results distinct.

Start benchmarking with the E1 feasibility pilot: static template, fixed Codex route, router disabled, deterministic oracle and no judge model. Run positive, valid scientific negative and missing-check-bundle pre-dispatch-stop cases three times each. Require nine run records with `pins_match: true`, nine score records and aggregates rebuilt byte-identically from score files. Host/launcher collects inventory before every test/repeat and samples execution peaks.

Then complete the S01–S06 M1 pilot using E1–E4 as designed; E2–E4 require the isolated evaluation profile. Keep E5 and later statistical campaigns outside M1 pilot acceptance. Deliver the explicitly requested E6 OpenJiuwen baseline support below separately from the pilot; do not defer it merely because E6 is not a pilot prerequisite. Preserve evidence and clean up only job-owned resources. Verify actual container connectivity and retrieval, report blocked/missing evidence honestly, and follow the native task/spec workflow.

## OpenJiuwen baseline adapter

Implement and verify communication with an upstream OpenJiuwen-based agent baseline through the design's E6 external-configuration adapter (`prepare`, `run`, `collect`). Inspect the actual upstream runtime and use its supported SDK, CLI or API; do not assume it implements AI4R's control API. Identify whether the baseline is OpenJiuwen agent-core or an upstream JiuwenSwarm harness, and pin its repository/commit, agent configuration and effective model/settings. Our modified AI4R branch is not the upstream baseline. Use the existing `plain_model_agent` configuration kind where appropriate; distinguish harness identity from model identity and reconcile any necessary contract changes in native task/interface records.

Keep the adapter in its own process/OS identity inside the sidecar, with the designed network policy and no label access or extra baseline container. The runner coordinates; the adapter invokes the baseline agent. Preserve equivalent case keys, visible inputs/resource snapshots, tool access, host profile and total budgets, including AI4R's checking/model-call overhead. Record unavoidable capability differences and exclude incomparable pairs instead of claiming a controlled comparison.

Collect real terminal outputs, artifacts, usage/timings where exposed, failures and exact pins into the common `run_record` format. Leave unavailable internal gate/role fields empty with explicit limitations; do not invent AI4R-style internals or penalize their absence. The separate referee evaluates terminal results with the same protected oracle. Support queued paired AI4R/baseline cases, retain both sides' evidence and report baseline coverage, exclusions and results separately. Verify an actual baseline invocation, evidence collection, timeout/cancellation behavior and an unavailable-baseline case. Missing runtime/model access is BLOCKED, never a mock baseline or a comparative pass. Deliver this adapter as requested, without making it a prerequisite for the existing E1 pilot or core M1 product acceptance.

## Long queues and reviewable acceptance evidence

Support long, finite, data-driven queues of independently defined cases, executed sequentially as designed. Cases specify visible tasks, supplied resources/setup, ordered actions, timeouts and evidence requirements without hardcoding particular scenarios into the apparatus. Persist progress and correlate case/version, repeat, request, app run and target/build identities. Reconcile interrupted submissions and resume observation without silently rerunning product work. Bound campaign duration/storage, save completed records incrementally, and explicitly account for unfinished, blocked or inconclusive cases. Never skip cases to obtain a passing matrix.

For each case, export a structured record and readable review sheet with **Inputs and Setup** and **Actual Output and Observations**. Retain actual inputs/resource hashes, effective configuration/environment, per-step requests and observations, output artifacts and provenance references, check/gate decisions, downstream action or refusal, terminal reason, timings and limitations. Link authorized criteria to the exact evidence supporting or contradicting them; missing evidence stays explicit. A reviewer must be able to assess the case from these records rather than a generated success narrative or final report alone. Complete any missing designed export through its owning contract; do not settle for a summary or bypass access controls. Report unavailable evidence honestly.

Keep execution, independent benchmark scoring and report generation separate. Ordinary client-validation expectations stay in case files; protected benchmark labels, defect annotations, rubrics and expected answers remain referee-only. Do not expose hidden test specifics through product/model inputs or this generic coder handoff. Support varied workflows, resource the tconditions and output obligations without embedding the supplied example or its thresholds. Queue recovery is transport/observation recovery, not automatic repair or the later long-horizon benchmark family.
